{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"O14543","secondaryAccessions":["O14509"],"uniProtkbId":"SOCS3_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2002-04-16","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"1998-01-01","entryVersion":210,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"11071852"}],"value":"Suppressor of cytokine signaling 3"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"11071852"}],"value":"SOCS-3"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Cytokine-inducible SH2 protein 3"},"shortNames":[{"value":"CIS-3"}]},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"9266833"}],"value":"STAT-induced STAT inhibitor 3"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"9266833"}],"value":"SSI-3"}]}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:19391"}],"value":"SOCS3"},"synonyms":[{"value":"CIS3"},{"value":"SSI3"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"O35718"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15601820"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16459330"}],"value":"SOCS family proteins form part of a classical negative feedback system that regulates cytokine signal transduction. SOCS3 is involved in negative regulation of cytokines that signal through the JAK/STAT pathway (PubMed:16459330). Inhibits signal transduction by binding to transmembrane signaling receptors including IL6ST/gp130, LIFR, EPOR, INSR, IL12RB2, CSF3R/G-CSF-R and LEPR. Binding to JAK2 inhibits its kinase activity and regulates IL6 signaling. Suppresses fetal liver erythropoiesis. Regulates onset and maintenance of allergic responses mediated by T-helper type 2 cells (By similarity). Probable substrate recognition component of a SCF-like ECS (Elongin BC-CUL2/5-SOCS-box protein) E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase complex which mediates the ubiquitination and subsequent proteasomal degradation of target proteins (PubMed:15601820). Upon OSM stimulation, negatively regulates the JAK-STAT signaling mediated through type II OSM receptor complex by interacting directly with JAK1 (PubMed:16459330)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"value":"Protein modification; protein ubiquitination"}],"commentType":"PATHWAY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"O35718"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10421843"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12027890"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"14559241"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15070676"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15601820"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16410555"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16459330"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23019338"}],"value":"Interacts with multiple activated proteins of the tyrosine kinase signaling pathway including IGF1 receptor, insulin receptor and JAK2. Binding to JAK2 is mediated through the KIR and SH2 domains to a phosphorylated tyrosine residue within the JAK2 JH1 domain (PubMed:10421843). Binds specific activated tyrosine residues of the leptin, EPO, IL12, GSCF and gp130 receptors (PubMed:12027890, PubMed:14559241). Interaction with CSNK1E stabilizes SOCS3 protein (PubMed:15070676). Component of the probable ECS(SOCS3) E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase complex which contains CUL5, RNF7/RBX2, Elongin BC complex and SOCS3 (PubMed:15601820). Interacts with CUL5, RNF7, ELOB and ELOC (PubMed:15601820). Interacts with CUL2 (PubMed:15601820). Interacts with FGFR3 (PubMed:16410555). Interacts with INSR (By similarity). Interacts with BCL10; this interaction may interfere with BCL10-binding with PELI2 (By similarity). Interacts with NOD2 (via CARD domain); the interaction promotes NOD2 degradation (PubMed:23019338). Interacts directly with JAK1 in an OSM stimulation-dependent manner; this interaction negatively regulates the JAK-STAT signaling mediated through type II OSM receptor complex (PubMed:16459330)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P51451","geneName":"BLK","intActId":"EBI-2105445"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q13480","geneName":"GAB1","intActId":"EBI-517684"},"numberOfExperiments":4,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q8N8K9","geneName":"KIAA1958","intActId":"EBI-10181113"},"numberOfExperiments":6,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P10721","geneName":"KIT","intActId":"EBI-1379503"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q66K74","geneName":"MAP1S","intActId":"EBI-2133734"},"numberOfExperiments":6,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"I6L996","geneName":"PTK2","intActId":"EBI-10181089"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O95863","geneName":"SNAI1","intActId":"EBI-1045459"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P42681","geneName":"TXK","intActId":"EBI-7877438"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14543","intActId":"EBI-714146"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P07947","geneName":"YES1","intActId":"EBI-515331"},"numberOfExperiments":6,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"texts":[{"value":"Widely expressed with high expression in heart, placenta, skeletal muscle, peripheral blood leukocytes, fetal and adult lung, and fetal liver and kidney. Lower levels in thymus"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY"},{"texts":[{"value":"The ESS and SH2 domains are required for JAK phosphotyrosine binding. Further interaction with the KIR domain is necessary for signal and kinase inhibition"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250"}],"value":"The SOCS box domain mediates the interaction with the Elongin BC complex, an adapter module in different E3 ubiquitin ligase complexes"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"value":"Phosphorylated on tyrosine residues after stimulation by the cytokines, IL-2, EPO or IGF1"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"commentType":"DISEASE","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16685656"}],"value":"There is some evidence that SOCS3 may be a susceptibility gene for atopic dermatitis linked to 17q25. SOCS3 messenger RNA is significantly more highly expressed in skin from patients with atopic dermatitis than in skin from healthy controls. Furthermore, a genetic association between atopic dermatitis and a haplotype in the SOCS3 gene has been found in two independent groups of patients"}]}},{"commentType":"WEB RESOURCE","r